A||||9||mrtgman||NEED HELP FAST WITH HEADLIGHT MOTOR!||||8||
Z||000000||mrtgman||10-22-2001||07:27 PM||||I just got home and turned my headlights off but the right ones motor keeps running. The round knob on top of the motor keeps spinning! How can I shut this thing off? I can't find a fuse or anything. It's an 86 gt if that matters.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierofront1_1.jpg">   86 gt owned since new!<A HREF="http://www.palmbeachloan.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.palmbeachloan.com</A>||||reg||8
Z||000001||WampusCat||10-22-2001||07:40 PM||||The wires coming from the motor should have a connector a few inches from the motor that you can unplug.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrtgman||10-22-2001||08:26 PM||||Well I ended up wedging a piece of plastic between the knob and the headlight motor mount. Has this ever happened to anyone else?<P>Weird!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierofront1_1.jpg">   86 gt owned since new!<A HREF="http://www.palmbeachloan.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.palmbeachloan.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||David Bartlett||10-22-2001||08:31 PM||||Yea happened to me. Open up the headlight motor casing and flip the largest gear around. The headlight only uses half of the gear.. This will fix your problem.  Oh year re-grease and re-silicone the motor casing.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||G-Nasty||10-23-2001||01:30 AM||||If you still have problems...let me know<BR>I've got several actuator motors and some extra rodneys kits 4 sale-cheap!<BR>Junk yards charge about 50 ea (if u can find)<BR>I will sell working actuators for 25 ea||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fierozilla||10-23-2001||01:52 AM||||Pull the fuse for a temp fix. Fuse also runs dash lights, so you'll lose those. Take the motor apart and reposition the wheel (with the teeth). The wheel stops in the same place and the "teeth" have worn down in the stop area due to time and use. (Like David Bartlett said). Pretty easy fix.<p>[This message has been edited by Fierozilla (edited 10-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||SLYGUY||10-23-2001||03:32 AM||||Take it apart and check the "bushings".<BR>These were worn out on mine. When I bought the car the left headlight would dance around a lot and then finally make it to it's full up position. After using the headlights a few times, it totally quit. Motor would run for about 10-15 seconds when I powered up or down.<P>Bought the rebuild kits from Rodney. I think I paid $8 for both sides. Only used one kit.<P>Take the whole assembly apart with the detailed instrucitons. You will find the gear, and possibly a fine white powder. The powder is what is left of your 'bushings'.<BR>I replaced them (3) in about 20 minutes and have worked great ever since.<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000007||WampusCat||10-23-2001||07:11 AM||||His is an '86.  Only '87-88 have "the bushings."||||reg||1
